# Header self-sufficiency / missing-include fixes for JavaScriptCore.
# Merged from 14 patches: webkit-jsc-glib-export-macros,
# webkit-jsc-assembler-platform, webkit-jsc-cpu-b3-includes,
# webkit-jsc-b3-export-macros, webkit-jsc-b3-platform, webkit-jsc-b3-cstdint,
# webkit-jsc-bytecode-platform, webkit-jsc-dfg-platform,
# webkit-jsc-ftl-platform, webkit-jsc-heap-cstddef,
# webkit-jsc-inspector-remote-glib, webkit-jsc-jit-platform,
# webkit-jsc-lol-platform, webkit-jsc-wasm-platform.
#
# Same single class as webkit-portability-wtf-pal, across B3/Air, bytecode, DFG,
# FTL, JIT, LOL, Wasm, heap and the GLib/remote-inspector headers: import
# wtf/Platform.h where ENABLE()/USE() appear in top-level guards,
# JSExportMacros.h where JS_EXPORT_PRIVATE is declared, <cstdint>/<cstddef>
# where fixed-width types and size_t are used. Purely mechanical, and by far the
# largest patch in the stack (~1100 files) — it is also the one that breaks on
# every WPE bump.
#
# See the MAINTENANCE note in webkit-portability-wtf-pal: regenerate, do not
# hand-fix, and prefer the force-include prelude (STREAMLINE-PLAN A1).
#
# ---
